  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agricultural Support in Somalia through IFAD</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">IFAD Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Ausgleich der Zahlungsr&#xfc;ckst&#xe4;nde Somalias bei IFAD, um neue IFAD Projekte in Somalia zu erm&#xf6;glichen und so einen Beitrag zur Nahrungsmittelproduktion und Ern&#xe4;hrungssicherung zu leisten.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia is affected by a severe food crisis, both acute and structural, and at the same time lacks financial resources and funding partners to address this crisis. Somalia is a founding member of the International Fund for Agricultural Development (IFAD), but is unable to benefit from its services due to arrears. A grant of EUR 6 million will partially cover these arrears, as well as future repayments. This will enable IFAD to implement agricultural development projects in Somalia again. The target group of the project is the rural population in regions of Somalia particularly affected by hunger and poverty.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia is affected by a severe food crisis, both acute and structural, and at the same time lacks financial resources and funding partners to address this crisis. Somalia is a founding member of the International Fund for Agricultural Development (IFAD), but is unable to benefit from its services due to arrears. A grant of EUR 6 million will partially cover these arrears, as well as future repayments. This will enable IFAD to implement agricultural development projects in Somalia again. The target group of the project is the rural population in regions of Somalia particularly affected by hunger and poverty.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Somalia ist sowohl akut als auch strukturell von einer schweren Ern&#xe4;hrungskrise betroffen, gleichzeitig fehlen finanzielle Mittel und Finanzierungspartner, um der Krise entgegenzuwirken. Somalia ist Gr&#xfc;ndungsmitglied des International Fund for Agricultural Development (IFAD), kann aber aufgrund von Zahlungsr&#xfc;ckst&#xe4;nden nicht von dessen Leistungen profitieren. &#xdc;ber einen Zuschuss von EUR 6 Mio. werden diese Zahlungsr&#xfc;ckst&#xe4;nde, sowie zuk&#xfc;nftige Tilgungen teilweise beglichen. Damit wird IFAD bef&#xe4;higt wieder Projekte zur landwirtschaftlichen Entwicklung in Somalia umzusetzen. Zielgruppe des Vorhabens ist die l&#xe4;ndliche Bev&#xf6;lkerung in besonders von Hunger und Armut betroffenen Regionen Somalias.</narrative>
  </description>
